PATCH 551: two more `word == -1` constant-false sentinels.

Same class as patch 548: `DAT_2000_...` declared `undefined2` is a `uint16_t`, which promotes to `int`,
so a Ghidra-emitted `== -1` can never be true and the guard is dead.  board:0022 carries the class.

## DGROUP:0x9fd9 -- four sites, one word

The image contains exactly seven references to the displacement, and every one is word-width:

    bddd: c7 06 d9 9f ff ff  movw  $0xffff,0x9fd9
    be00: 8b 1e d9 9f        mov   0x9fd9,%bx
    be0e: 3b 1e d9 9f        cmp   0x9fd9,%bx
    be14: 83 3e d9 9f ff     cmpw  $0xffff,0x9fd9
    be25: 89 1e d9 9f        mov   %bx,0x9fd9
    be6e: c7 06 d9 9f ff ff  movw  $0xffff,0x9fd9
    c096: 83 3e d9 9f ff     cmpw  $0xffff,0x9fd9

The declaration is already right; only the constant was wrong.  The port's four `== -1`/`!= -1` sites
map onto the two `cmpw $0xffff` compares -- two pairs of Ghidra functions share a tail, the same way
`FUN_0000_bee2` and `FUN_0000_bee8` both fall through to 0xbeef.

## DGROUP:0x6db6 -- the wraparound arm of a list-cycling loop

0x6db6 is a genuine word (`incw`, `decw`, `cmpw`, `movw $0xffff,0x6db6` at 0x1bef3).  The loop that
steps the list BACKWARDS reads:

    1bf16: ff 0e b6 6d       decw  0x6db6
    1bf1a: a1 b6 6d          mov   0x6db6,%ax
    1bf1d: 3d ff ff          cmp   $0xffff,%ax
    1bf20: 75 08             jne   0x1bf2a          ; no underflow -> use this index
    1bf22: a1 d0 6d          mov   0x6dd0,%ax       ; underflowed -> wrap to the end ...
    1bf25: a3 b6 6d          mov   %ax,0x6db6
    1bf28: eb ec             jmp   0x1bf16          ; ... and step again

The port's `if (DAT_2000_2db6 != -1) break;` was always true, so the break was always taken and the
wraparound arm was unreachable: stepping backwards off the start of the list could never wrap to its
end.

board:0022

